course: dictionary
lesson: 3953
title: Funny: laugh, strange or unwell
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: The word funny has three main meanings, and the words around it tell you which one you need. «The clown told a funny joke and the whole class laughed.» Here funny means making you laugh or smile.
explain: Funny can also mean strange or unusual. «There is a funny smell coming from the kitchen.» Nobody is laughing here. The smell is odd, and a funny smell like gas or burning is a reason to tell an adult straight away.
explain: Funny can mean feeling a bit unwell too. «I feel funny after that ride, so I need to sit down.» Check the clues: sitting down and feeling odd point to unwell, not to laughing. Always swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: «Funny» means making you laugh or smile, as in «a funny joke».
fact: «Funny» can mean strange or unusual, as in «a funny smell», and a strange smell like gas or burning means you should tell an adult.
fact: «Funny» can also mean feeling a bit unwell, as in «I feel funny».
fact: «Funnier» and «funniest» are the comparing forms: «funnier» is more funny than something else, «funniest» is the most funny of all.
fact: A joke is only truly funny if everyone can laugh, including the person it is about. A joke that hurts someone is not funny.
exercise: «The clown wore big shoes and told a funny joke.» What does funny mean here? | Very cold | Sad and quiet | Hard to lift | *Making you laugh
exercise: «There is a funny smell coming from the kitchen, so tell an adult.» What does funny mean here? | Happy and bright | Very tasty | A joke you like | *Strange or unusual, and maybe a sign of danger
exercise: Ellie says, «I felt funny after the ride, so I sat down.» What does funny mean here? | Feeling very cold | Feeling like laughing | *Feeling a bit unwell | Feeling brave
test: «That was the ___ story I have ever heard!» Which word fits best? | funnily | funnier | *funniest | funny
test: In the talk of this lesson, «I'm dead» means what? | *That's so funny | I am very tired | I am lost | I have died
exam: Mia tells a joke that makes her friend cry. Is the joke funny? | Yes, because it is a joke | *No, because a joke is only funny if the person it is about can laugh too | Yes, because jokes are always funny | Yes, because Mia laughed
